      "text": "\\[\n\\begin{aligned}\n(2x - 5)(x + 7) - (x + 5)(2x - 1) &= 2x \\cdot x + 2x \\cdot 7 - 5 \\cdot x - 5 \\cdot 7 - (2x \\cdot 2x + 2x \\cdot (-1) - 5 \\cdot 2x - 5 \\cdot (-1)) \\\\\n&= 2x^2 + 14x - 5x - 35 - (4x^2 - 2x - 10x + 5) \\\\\n&= 2x^2 + 9x - 35 - (4x^2 - 12x + 5) \\\\\n&= 2x^2 + 9x - 35 - 4x^2 + 12x - 5 \\\\\n&= (-4x^2) + (2x^2) + (9x + 12x) + (-35 - 5) \\\\\n&= -2x^2 + 21x - 40.\n\\end{aligned}\n\\]\nTherefore, the simplified expression is: \\boxed{-2x^2 + 21x - 40}.\n\nTo solve the given expression \\((2x - 5)(x + 7) - (x + 5)(2x - 1)\\), we will expand both products and then simplify the resulting expression step by step.\n\nFirst, let's expand \\((2x - 5)(x + 7)\\):\n\n\\[\n(2x - 5)(x + 7) = 2x \\cdot x + 2x \\cdot 7 - 5 \\cdot x - 5 \\cdot 7 = 2x^2 + 14x - 5x - 35 = 2x^2 + 9x - 35\n\\]\n\nNext, let's expand \\((x + 5)(2x - 1)\\):\n\n\\[\n(x + 5)(2x - 1) = x \\cdot 2x + x \\cdot (-1) + 5 \\cdot 2x + 5 \\cdot (-1) = 2x^2 - x + 10x - 5 = 2x^2 + 9x - 5\n\\]\n\nNow, we substitute these expansions back into the original expression:\n\n\\[\n(2x - 5)(x + 7) - (x + 5)(2x - 1) = (2x^2 + 9x - 35) - (2x^2 + 9x - 5)\n\\]\n\nNext, we distribute the negative sign through the second set of parentheses:\n\n\\[\n2x^2 + 9x - 35 - 2x^2 - 9x + 5\n\\]\n\nNow, we combine like terms:\n\n\\[\n(2x^2 - 2x^2) + (9x - 9x) + (-35 + 5) = 0 + 0 - 30 = -30\n\\]\n\nThus, the simplified expression is:\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{-30}\n\\]",
