      "text": "We'll begin by expanding the given expression $(2x - 5)(x + 7) - (x + 5)(2x - 1)$ using the distributive property.\n\nFirst, let's expand $(2x - 5)(x + 7)$:\n\\[\n(2x - 5)(x + 7) = 2x(x) + 2x(7) - 5(x) - 5(7)\n\\]\n\\[\n= 2x^2 + 14x - 5x - 35\n\\]\n\\[\n= 2x^2 + 9x - 35\n\\]\n\nNext, let's expand $(x + 5)(2x - 1)$:\n\\[\n(x + 5)(2x - 1) = x(2x) + x(-1) + 5(2x) + 5(-1)\n\\]\n\\[\n= 2x^2 - x + 10x - 5\n\\]\n\\[\n= 2x^2 + 9x - 5\n\\]\n\nNow, we substitute these expansions back into the original expression:\n\\[\n(2x^2 + 9x - 35) - (2x^2 + 9x - 5)\n\\]\n\nNext, we distribute the negative sign through the second polynomial:\n\\[\n2x^2 + 9x - 35 - 2x^2 - 9x + 5\n\\]\n\nWe can now combine like terms:\n\\[\n2x^2 - 2x^2 + 9x - 9x - 35 + 5\n\\]\n\\[\n= (2x^2 - 2x^2) + (9x - 9x) + (-35 + 5)\n\\]\n\\[\n= 0 + 0 - 30\n\\]\n\\[\n= -30\n\\]\n\nTherefore, the simplified expression is:\n\\[\n\\boxed{-30}\n\\]",
