      "sample_index": 3,
      "text": "To solve the problem \\((2x - 5)(x + 7) - (x + 5)(2x - 1)\\), we will first expand each product separately and then combine the results.\n\n### Step 1: Expand \\((2x - 5)(x + 7)\\)\n\nUsing the distributive property (FOIL method):\n\\[\n(2x - 5)(x + 7) = 2x \\cdot x + 2x \\cdot 7 - 5 \\cdot x - 5 \\cdot 7\n\\]\n\\[\n= 2x^2 + 14x - 5x - 35\n\\]\n\\[\n= 2x^2 + 9x - 35\n\\]\n\n### Step 2: Expand \\((x + 5)(2x - 1)\\)\n\nUsing the distributive property (FOIL method):\n\\[\n(x + 5)(2x - 1) = x \\cdot 2x + x \\cdot (-1) + 5 \\cdot 2x + 5 \\cdot (-1)\n\\]\n\\[\n= 2x^2 - x + 10x - 5\n\\]\n\\[\n= 2x^2 + 9x - 5\n\\]\n\n### Step 3: Subtract the second expanded expression from the first\n\n\\[\n(2x^2 + 9x - 35) - (2x^2 + 9x - 5)\n\\]\n\nDistribute the negative sign through the second set of parentheses:\n\\[\n= 2x^2 + 9x - 35 - 2x^2 - 9x + 5\n\\]\n\nCombine like terms:\n\\[\n= (2x^2 - 2x^2) + (9x - 9x) + (-35 + 5)\n\\]\n\\[\n= 0 + 0 - 30\n\\]\n\\[\n= -30\n\\]\n\nThus, the simplified form of \\((2x - 5)(x + 7) - (x + 5)(2x - 1)\\) is \\(\\boxed{-30}\\).",
